# DEC-1 (DECISIONS (1).md, "Corpus storage — BLOCKING, day 1"): "The captured
# corpus never enters git — not the repository, not Git-LFS. Payload lives on
# disk outside version control. A committed index records what was captured."
# INDEX.jsonl is that committed index and is explicitly un-ignored below.
#
# Order matters: `corpus/*` (not bare `corpus/`) excludes the directory's
# contents without excluding the directory itself — a bare `corpus/` rule
# would exclude the directory, and no `!` exception inside an excluded
# directory can ever match.
corpus/*
!corpus/INDEX.jsonl

# Downloaded input for tools/capture/ (Tranco top-10k list, 186,894 bytes).
# Regenerable, not a copy of anything in spec/, does not belong in git.
tools/capture/tranco_top10k.csv
